\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My God, I thank Thee, who hast made
\par The earth so bright,
\par So full of splendour and of joy,
\par Beauty and light;
\par So many glorious things are here,
\par Noble and right.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I thank Thee, too, that Thou hast made
\par Joy to abound,
\par So many gentle thoughts and deeds
\par Circling us round,
\par That in the darkest spot of earth
\par Some love is found.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I thank Thee more that all our joy
\par Is touched with pain, 
\par That shadows fall on brightest hours,
\par That thorns remain,
\par So that earth's bliss may be our guide,
\par And not our chain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I thank Thee, Lord, that Thou hast kept
\par The best in store:
\par We have enough, yet not too much
\par To long for more-
\par A yearning for a deeper peace
\par Not known before.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I thank Thee, Lord, that here our souls,
\par Though amply blest,
\par Can never find, although they seek,
\par A perfect rest,
\par Nor ever shall, until they lean 
\par On jesu's breast.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

